-- CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-4 (2026-10-26, pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000214, CHAOS-DRILL-FAILED-1: control:control-alternate-probes; follows migrations/2026-10-19-control-alternate-probes.sql, -probes2 and -probes3)
--
-- WHAT WAS MEASURED (qnfo-audit SELECT only, 2026-10-26 18:10-18:40Z)
--   The probe of the control control-alternate-probes (the alternate of the drill set itself) reads v_control_alternate_untested.controls_untested_without_probe and fails while it is above 0:
--   the drill said "a control with an alternate has no probe and no tested date" at 13:01Z, and the detector contract fm-control-alternate-undrilled reads fail for the same count. Read live: 18.
--   v_control_alternate_status lists them as drill_state no-probe with alternate_tested_at NULL: research-repo-archive-gate, research-repo-sync-switches, email-filter-journal-pitch-senders,
--   dash-owner-decision-session-gate, pn-r2-filer-quiet-gate, metric-playbook-recovery-hold and twelve breach-doctor controls (caps, taint-guard, action-allowlist, gap-measure, gap-caps,
--   own-issue-guard, strike-cap, auto-demotion, age-gate, tool-exclusion-rule, secret-change-measure, rearm-capacity). All registered in the last day, each with a written alternate_path and no probe.
--   The register stamps alternate_tested_at only from a passing probe (CHAOS-DRILL-1 second pass), and a hand-written date is the thing CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-1 exists to remove, so no date is
--   written here: each control gets one read-only probe and the next 6-hourly drill stamps it if the probe passes.
--
-- WHAT EACH PROBE IS
--   One row per control in control_alternate_probes in the chaosJudge shape (SELECT 'ok' AS expected, CASE ... END AS observed): observed is a reason string when the named alternate is missing or
--   in the wrong state, 'ok' otherwise. Each probe reads the lever its control_registry.alternate_path names (the ops_config key exists and holds a value the code reads, the breach_playbooks row
--   exists, is enabled and is in the stated mode, the view, trigger or detector contract it names exists and is active) and the evidence of the control itself (the invariant the control enforces
--   still holds in the data: no archive request before 3 consolidated deposits, no playbook write outside the allowlist, no rule demoted past its release, no gap issue over the cap).
--   Every probe was run read-only against live qnfo-audit before it was written here and reads ok now. Two first drafts failed on live and were corrected, not loosened: the action-allowlist probe
--   matched the table name metric_registry inside a read (a SELECT of PB-T4) and now matches a write target only (after INTO or before SET), and the email-filter probe applied the full-address rule to
--   two older domain-pattern sender filters (ids 14 and 15, priority 0) that are another family, so it now reads the priority-50 tier of this control. No probe contains an e-mail address.
--   A probe cannot pass by being empty: the offline suite breaks every clause of every probe on a fixture of the live schemas and the probe reads the reason, and mutation checks of the probe texts
--   were each caught. Windows are stated in each window_note (state probes have none; the doctor tick is 30 minutes, a demotion 120, the repo-sync tick 7 days because it logs nothing while the
--   target is legacy, the evaluator's recovered rows 7 days).
--
-- NOT DONE HERE, ON PURPOSE
--   No alternate_tested_at is written (the drill stamps it), no probe is edited, no control or playbook changes. The root cause of the recurring issue is that controls are registered
--   without a probe (18 in one day by several sessions): fm-control-alternate-undrilled already files within the hour, and a migration lint is the structural fix, noted in the decision row.
--
-- The table bak_20261026_control_probes4_evidence holds the evidence text of the 18 controls first. The Rollback line below does not read it: it removes the probe rows that never ran, restores
-- the evidence by replacing the appended note and clears alternate_tested_at, which was NULL for all 18 when this file was written. Every statement is guarded so a second apply changes nothing.
--
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- BACKUP: bak_20261026_control_probes4_evidence
-- Rollback: DELETE FROM control_alternate_probes WHERE control IN ('research-repo-archive-gate', 'research-repo-sync-switches', 'breach-doctor-caps', 'breach-doctor-taint-guard', 'breach-doctor-action-allowlist', 'breach-doctor-gap-measure', 'breach-doctor-gap-caps', 'breach-doctor-own-issue-guard', 'breach-doctor-strike-cap', 'email-filter-journal-pitch-senders', 'dash-owner-decision-session-gate', 'breach-doctor-auto-demotion', 'breach-doctor-age-gate', 'breach-doctor-tool-exclusion-rule', 'breach-doctor-secret-change-measure', 'breach-doctor-rearm-capacity', 'metric-playbook-recovery-hold', 'pn-r2-filer-quiet-gate') AND last_run_at IS NULL; UPDATE control_registry SET evidence = replace(evidence, ' | CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-4 2026-10-26: probed by its control_alternate_probes row (a state probe on the lever the alternate names and on the evidence of the control), judged by the chaos drill, which alone stamps alternate_tested_at.', ''), alternate_tested_at = NULL WHERE control IN ('research-repo-archive-gate', 'research-repo-sync-switches', 'breach-doctor-caps', 'breach-doctor-taint-guard', 'breach-doctor-action-allowlist', 'breach-doctor-gap-measure', 'breach-doctor-gap-caps', 'breach-doctor-own-issue-guard', 'breach-doctor-strike-cap', 'email-filter-journal-pitch-senders', 'dash-owner-decision-session-gate', 'breach-doctor-auto-demotion', 'breach-doctor-age-gate', 'breach-doctor-tool-exclusion-rule', 'breach-doctor-secret-change-measure', 'breach-doctor-rearm-capacity', 'metric-playbook-recovery-hold', 'pn-r2-filer-quiet-gate')
-- Rollback note: decision_log stays (append-only); a probe row that has already run is kept by the Rollback (last_run_at IS NOT NULL) and is disabled by hand.

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_control_probes4_evidence AS
  SELECT control, evidence, alternate_tested_at FROM control_registry WHERE control IN ('research-repo-archive-gate', 'research-repo-sync-switches', 'breach-doctor-caps', 'breach-doctor-taint-guard', 'breach-doctor-action-allowlist', 'breach-doctor-gap-measure', 'breach-doctor-gap-caps', 'breach-doctor-own-issue-guard', 'breach-doctor-strike-cap', 'email-filter-journal-pitch-senders', 'dash-owner-decision-session-gate', 'breach-doctor-auto-demotion', 'breach-doctor-age-gate', 'breach-doctor-tool-exclusion-rule', 'breach-doctor-secret-change-measure', 'breach-doctor-rearm-capacity', 'metric-playbook-recovery-hold', 'pn-r2-filer-quiet-gate');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO control_alternate_probes (control, probe_sql, window_note, enabled) VALUES
 ('research-repo-archive-gate',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_repo_archive'') = 0 THEN ''the ops_config row research_repo_archive is missing, so the off lever cannot be set'' WHEN (SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_repo_archive'') NOT IN (''on'', ''off'') THEN ''ops_config research_repo_archive holds a value other than on or off, and only the exact value off stops the archive request'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM portfolio_actions WHERE action = ''archive-request'' AND repo IN (''QNFO/qnfo-ensemble-research'', ''qnfo-ensemble-research'')) AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM research_run_ledger WHERE status = ''ok'' AND repo = ''QNFO/qnfo-research'') < 3 THEN ''an archive request for the legacy ensemble repository exists while research_run_ledger holds fewer than 3 consolidated deposits, so the gate did not hold'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe, no window: the lever row and its value, and the gate''s own rule (no archive request for QNFO/qnfo-ensemble-research before 3 consolidated deposits are ledgered). The archive itself is reversible on GitHub and nothing is deleted, which no D1 read can show', 1),
 ('research-repo-sync-switches',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ops_config WHERE key IN (''research_repo_sync'', ''research_repo_restore'', ''research_repo_target'')) < 3 THEN ''an ops_config row of the three repo levers (research_repo_sync, research_repo_restore, research_repo_target) is missing, so a switch cannot be set'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ops_config WHERE key IN (''research_repo_sync'', ''research_repo_restore'') AND value NOT IN (''on'', ''off'')) THEN ''research_repo_sync or research_repo_restore holds a value other than on or off, and only the exact value off stops that step of the tick'' WHEN (SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_repo_target'') NOT IN (''auto'', ''legacy'', ''consolidated'') THEN ''ops_config research_repo_target holds a value other than auto, legacy or consolidated, which the resolver reads as auto'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind = ''repo-sync'' AND status IN (''ok'', ''warn'') AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-10080 minutes'')) THEN ''no repo-sync event in 7 days, so the 10-minute sync tick that the switches guard has not run'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '7 days for the sync tick (it logs repo-sync on every full tick, 62 events in the 24 hours to 2026-10-26 18:21Z, and logs nothing while the target is legacy or the token is missing, so a longer window is used); the three lever rows and their valid values are a state check', 1),
 ('breach-doctor-caps',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ops_config WHERE key IN (''breach_doctor_max_cases'', ''breach_doctor_max_actions'', ''breach_doctor_budget_ms'')) < 3 THEN ''an ops_config row of the three doctor caps (breach_doctor_max_cases, breach_doctor_max_actions, breach_doctor_budget_ms) is missing, so the bound is not a lever'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ops_config WHERE (key = ''breach_doctor_max_cases'' AND NOT (CAST(value AS INTEGER) BETWEEN 1 AND 60)) OR (key = ''breach_doctor_max_actions'' AND NOT (CAST(value AS INTEGER) BETWEEN 0 AND 20)) OR (key = ''breach_doctor_budget_ms'' AND NOT (CAST(value AS INTEGER) BETWEEN 5000 AND 40000))) THEN ''a doctor cap is outside the range bdConfig accepts (cases 1 to 60, actions 0 to 20, budget 5000 to 40000 ms), so the engine reads its default instead'' WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''breach_doctor''), ''measure'') <> ''off'' AND COALESCE((SELECT MAX(ts) FROM breach_diagnosis_events WHERE event = ''tick''), '''') < strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-30 minutes'') THEN ''the doctor wrote no tick event in 30 minutes while it is not switched off, so a cap that should only delay work has stopped the loop'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe on the three cap rows and their accepted ranges, plus 30 minutes for the doctor tick (it writes a tick event every 10 minutes, the shape of fm-breach-doctor-stalled): the alternate is backpressure, never a stop', 1),
 ('breach-doctor-taint-guard',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN COALESCE((SELECT last_refreshed FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''doctor_taint_violations_24h''), '''') < strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-180 minutes'') THEN ''the doctor_taint_violations_24h metric is missing or was not refreshed in 3 hours, so a refused free-text fact would go unreported'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''code_merge_trusted_sources'') THEN ''the ops_config row code_merge_trusted_sources is missing, so the trusted-source list the guard relies on is unreadable'' WHEN instr('','' || COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''code_merge_trusted_sources''), '''') || '','', '',*,'') > 0 OR instr('','' || COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''code_merge_trusted_sources''), '''') || '','', '',*|'') > 0 THEN ''code_merge_trusted_sources holds a global wildcard entry, so every source is trusted and the guard protects nothing'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '3 hours for the metric (refreshed every 10 minutes by the doctor tick), state check on the trusted-source list: the guard keeps free text out of a trusted doctor issue, the alternate is that the list stays a closed set and every refusal is counted', 1),
 ('breach-doctor-action-allowlist',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE enabled = 1 AND (instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''into ops_config'') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''ops_config set '') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''into human_actions'') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''human_actions set '') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''into decision_log'') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''decision_log set '') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''into fleet_tasks'') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''fleet_tasks set '') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''into fleet_crons'') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''fleet_crons set '') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''into control_registry'') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''control_registry set '') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''into metric_registry'') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''metric_registry set '') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''into breach_playbooks'') > 0 OR instr(lower(action_sql || revert_sql), ''breach_playbooks set '') > 0)) THEN ''an enabled playbook action or revert writes a table the write allowlist refuses (ops_config, human_actions, decision_log, fleet_tasks, fleet_crons, control_registry, metric_registry, breach_playbooks)'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks p, json_each(p.action_sql) s WHERE p.enabled = 1 AND p.action_kind = ''sql'' AND instr(s.value, ''?1'') = 0) THEN ''an enabled sql playbook has an action statement with no ?1 id predicate, which the allowlist requires of every statement'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe on the stored playbook texts, no window: the alternate is none (removing the allowlist would make a data row executable), so the probe reads what the allowlist keeps out of the data. The refusal cases themselves are pinned by qnfo-fleet-control/breach-doctor.test.mjs', 1),
 ('breach-doctor-gap-measure',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE rule_id = ''playbook-gap'' AND enabled = 1) THEN ''the playbook-gap row is missing or disabled, so the switch for the gap issues is not a lever'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = ''view'' AND name = ''v_breach_doctor_status'' AND instr(sql, ''unclassified_cases'') > 0 AND instr(sql, ''gap_families'') > 0 AND instr(sql, ''gap_by_family'') > 0) THEN ''v_breach_doctor_status no longer reports unclassified_cases, gap_families and gap_by_family, so the gap is hidden'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''breaches_undiagnosed_over_60m'') OR NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM analytics_metric_triggers WHERE metric_key = ''breaches_undiagnosed_over_60m'' AND enabled = 1) THEN ''the breaches_undiagnosed_over_60m metric or its enabled trigger is missing, so nobody is told about the gap'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe, no window: the lever row, the view columns that report the gap and the metric with its trigger that counts it; the case ledger rows (cause_class unclassified) are the data the view reads', 1),
 ('breach-doctor-gap-caps',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE rule_id = ''playbook-gap'' AND enabled = 1 AND max_per_tick BETWEEN 1 AND 12 AND max_per_day BETWEEN 1 AND 100) THEN ''the playbook-gap row is missing, disabled or has no bounded max_per_tick (1 to 12) and max_per_day (1 to 100), so the rate of gap issues is not bounded'' WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM agent_issues WHERE status = ''open'' AND title LIKE ''BREACH-DOCTOR-1: playbook gap %'') > 3 THEN ''more than 3 playbook gap issues are open, so BD_GAP_OPEN_MAX does not hold'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE status = ''open'' AND title LIKE ''BREACH-DOCTOR-1: playbook gap %'' AND substr(title, 31) IN (''OWNER-CHAT'', ''OWNER-REQUEST'', ''other'', ''BREACH-DOCTOR-1'')) THEN ''a playbook gap issue is open for a family no playbook can close (OWNER-CHAT, OWNER-REQUEST, other, BREACH-DOCTOR-1)'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe on the playbook-gap rate columns and on the open gap issues, no window: backpressure, the next family is filed when an open gap issue closes', 1),
 ('breach-doctor-own-issue-guard',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_diagnoses d JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = d.issue_id WHERE instr(a.title, ''BREACH-DOCTOR-1:'') = 1 AND d.state IN (''queued'', ''applied'', ''verifying'', ''verified'', ''failed'', ''reverted'')) THEN ''a playbook acted on an issue the doctor filed itself, which the own-issue guard forbids'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE instr(title, ''BREACH-DOCTOR-1: playbook gap BREACH-DOCTOR-1'') = 1) THEN ''a playbook gap issue was filed about the doctor own family'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND instr(a.title, ''BREACH-DOCTOR-1:'') = 1 AND a.created_at < (CAST(strftime(''%s'', ''now'') AS INTEGER) - 86400) * 1000 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_diagnoses d WHERE d.issue_id = a.id)) THEN ''an open doctor issue older than 24 hours has no breach_diagnoses row, so it is not classified or counted'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe on the case ledger, no window for the action and the gap family, 24 hours for the classification of an open own issue (the age gate and the per-tick case cap delay a first diagnosis by hours at most)', 1),
 ('breach-doctor-strike-cap',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE status = ''open'' AND instr(title, ''BREACH-DOCTOR-1: self '') = 1 GROUP BY title HAVING COUNT(*) > 1) THEN ''a BREACH-DOCTOR-1 self issue is open twice, so the dedupe on the open title is not holding'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_diagnoses WHERE state IN (''failed'', ''reverted'') AND last_progress_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-120 minutes'') GROUP BY issue_id HAVING COUNT(*) > 4) THEN ''one issue has more than 4 failed or reverted doctor cases in 120 minutes, so the strike cap and its 120-minute retry window do not hold'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '120 minutes for the strike window (3 failures, then one retry in 120 minutes) and a state check on the self issue titles; the retry rate is a code constant pinned by qnfo-fleet-control/breach-doctor.test.mjs, and the enabled switch that stops a rule is the column every playbook row carries', 1),
 ('email-filter-journal-pitch-senders',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM email_filters WHERE id IN (40, 41) AND field = ''sender'' AND action = ''spam'' AND priority = 50 AND enabled = 1 AND instr(pattern, ''@'') > 1 AND instr(pattern, ''%'') = 0) < 2 THEN ''a journal-pitch sender filter (email_filters 40 or 41) is missing, disabled or no longer a full sender address'' WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM email_filters WHERE id IN (26, 27, 28, 29, 30, 32, 33) AND action = ''spam'' AND enabled = 1) < 7 THEN ''one of the domain and body filters of the same family (email_filters 26 to 30, 32 and 33) is missing or disabled, so the second path for a new sender of the family is gone'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM email_filters WHERE field = ''sender'' AND action = ''spam'' AND priority = 50 AND enabled = 1 AND (instr(pattern, ''@'') < 2 OR instr(pattern, ''%'') > 0)) THEN ''an enabled priority-50 sender filter is not a full address, so it would match other senders'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe on email_filters ids 40 and 41 (the two filters of this control), 26 to 30, 32 and 33 (the domain filters that are the alternate) and on the shape of every priority-50 sender filter (the tier of the single-sender filters), no window; no address is written in this probe', 1),
 ('dash-owner-decision-session-gate',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = ''fm-owner-approval-without-handoff'' AND status = ''active'') THEN ''the fm-owner-approval-without-handoff detector contract is missing or not active, so an approval that skipped the e-mailed-code session would go unseen'' WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''default_approve_gate''), ''on'') NOT IN (''on'', ''off'') THEN ''ops_config default_approve_gate holds a value other than on or off, so the lever that decides the reversible cards by default is unreadable'' WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = ''view'' AND name IN (''v_human_action_gate'', ''v_human_action_decision'')) < 2 THEN ''v_human_action_gate or v_human_action_decision is missing, so the fleet has no reader that keeps an undecided card from blocking it'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe, no window: the alternate is that the fleet never waits on a decision, which rests on the detector contract that reads the approvals this gate lets through and on the two views and the lever that decide a reversible card by default; the gate cases themselves are pinned by qnfo-fleet-dashboard/cmd-decide.test.mjs', 1),
 ('breach-doctor-auto-demotion',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = ''fm-breach-doctor-rule-latched'' AND status = ''active'') THEN ''the fm-breach-doctor-rule-latched detector contract is missing or not active, so a demotion that outlives its release would go unseen'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE enabled = 1 AND mode = ''measure'' AND note LIKE ''demoted 20%'' AND substr(note, 9, 20) < strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-120 minutes'')) THEN ''a playbook has stayed demoted to measure for over 120 minutes, so the automatic release after 60 minutes did not run'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE enabled = 1 AND mode = ''on'') THEN ''no enabled playbook is in mode on, so the doctor acts on nothing and every rule reads as held'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '120 minutes for a demotion (release after 60 minutes plus one tick, the same bound as fm-breach-doctor-rule-latched) and state checks on the detector and on the rules', 1),
 ('breach-doctor-age-gate',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT (CAST(COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''breach_doctor_min_age_min''), ''-1'') AS INTEGER) BETWEEN 10 AND 120) THEN ''ops_config breach_doctor_min_age_min is missing or outside 10 to 120 minutes, so the gate is not a lever or exceeds the SLA-120M-1 ceiling'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''breaches_undiagnosed_over_60m'') THEN ''the breaches_undiagnosed_over_60m metric is not registered, so an issue past the age gate is not counted'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM analytics_metric_triggers WHERE metric_key = ''breaches_undiagnosed_over_60m'' AND enabled = 1) THEN ''the breaches_undiagnosed_over_60m metric has no enabled trigger, so a breach of it files nothing'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe, no window: the age gate is a minute count between 10 and 120 that a migration changes with its note, and the metric with its trigger flags every issue 60 minutes past the gate and never later than 120', 1),
 ('breach-doctor-tool-exclusion-rule',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = ''view'' AND name = ''tool_failures_excluded_24h'') THEN ''the tool_failures_excluded_24h view is missing, so excluded errors are no longer listed'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = ''fm-tool-exclusion-hides-outage'' AND status = ''active'') THEN ''the fm-tool-exclusion-hides-outage detector contract is missing or not active, so an exclusion that hides an outage would go unseen'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE rule_id = ''TL-R03-exclude'' AND enabled = 1 AND length(revert_sql) > 20 AND instr(trigger_sql, ''tool_error_exclusions'') > 0) THEN ''the TL-R03-exclude rule is missing, disabled, has no revert or no longer reads tool_error_exclusions'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe, no window: the view that lists every excluded row, the detector that reads an outage hidden by an exclusion, and the rule row with its revert; the surge guard itself is pinned by qnfo-fleet-control/breach-doctor-tool-loop.test.mjs', 1),
 ('breach-doctor-secret-change-measure',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE rule_id = ''TL-R07-secret'' AND enabled = 1 AND mode = ''measure'') THEN ''the TL-R07-secret rule is missing, disabled or no longer in measure, so the hold this control records was lifted without the register being updated'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_diagnoses WHERE rule_id = ''TL-R07-secret'' AND (mode = ''on'' OR state IN (''queued'', ''applied'', ''verifying'', ''verified''))) THEN ''a TL-R07-secret case acted (mode on or an action state) while the rule is held in measure'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND instr(a.title, ''SECRET-CHANGE-OBSERVED: '') = 1 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN (''active'', ''holding'', ''monitoring''))) THEN ''an open SECRET-CHANGE-OBSERVED issue has no live contract, so the rule in measure leaves it with no closer'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe, no window: the rule is held in measure, so it records the would-do case and acts on nothing, and the open SECRET-CHANGE-OBSERVED issues keep their own contracts and the filing loop that closes them', 1),
 ('breach-doctor-rearm-capacity',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE rule_id = ''TL-R01-rearm'' AND enabled = 1) THEN ''the TL-R01-rearm rule is missing or disabled, so the enabled switch that stops it is not a lever'' WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM breach_diagnoses WHERE rule_id = ''TL-R01-rearm'' AND state IN (''queued'', ''applied'', ''verifying'')) > 6 THEN ''more than 6 TL-R01-rearm cases are in flight, so the capacity cap does not hold'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''code_plan_daily_cap'' AND value NOT GLOB ''[0-9]*'') THEN ''ops_config code_plan_daily_cap is not a number, so the rule trigger reads the default of 24 instead of the planner cap'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_diagnoses WHERE rule_id = ''TL-R01-rearm'' AND state IN (''queued'', ''applied'', ''verifying'') AND lease_until < strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-60 minutes'')) THEN ''a TL-R01-rearm case is more than 60 minutes past its 30-minute lease, so the lease expiry did not end it'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '60 minutes past a 30-minute lease for an in-flight case, state checks on the cap of 6 in flight and on the planner daily cap value the trigger reads: backpressure, the rule resumes at 00:00Z or when a case ends', 1),
 ('metric-playbook-recovery-hold',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE rule_id = ''MD-4'' AND enabled = 1 AND instr(trigger_sql, ''* 1440 >= 120'') > 0) THEN ''the MD-4 rule is missing, disabled or its recovery gate is no longer 120 minutes (the SLA-120M-1 ceiling)'' WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''breach_doctor''), ''measure'') NOT IN (''on'', ''measure'', ''off'') THEN ''ops_config breach_doctor holds a value other than on, measure or off, so the lever that removes the gate without a deploy is unreadable'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM analytics_action_log WHERE status = ''recovered'' AND fired_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-10080 minutes'')) THEN ''the evaluator closed no recovered METRIC-TRIGGER issue in 7 days, so the TRIGGER-RECOVERY-1 path that the gate defers to is not running'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  '7 days for the evaluator own recovered rows (the path that closes at 60 minutes regardless of the gate) and state checks on the MD-4 gate text and on the doctor switch', 1),
 ('pn-r2-filer-quiet-gate',
  'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE rule_id = ''PN-R2'' AND enabled = 1) THEN ''the PN-R2 rule is missing or disabled, so the enabled switch that stops it is not a lever'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE rule_id = ''PN-R2'' AND instr(trigger_sql, ''1440'') > 0) THEN ''the PN-R2 trigger carries a 1440-minute window again, which SLA-120M-1 forbids'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE rule_id = ''PN-R2'' AND instr(trigger_sql, ''BREACH-DOCTOR-1: PN-R2 qnfo-fleet-control'') = 0) THEN ''the PN-R2 trigger no longer reads the lever issue BREACH-DOCTOR-1: PN-R2 qnfo-fleet-control, so the gate has no release condition'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_playbooks WHERE rule_id = ''PN-R2'' AND instr(verify_sql, ''pn-reopened'') = 0) THEN ''the PN-R2 verify no longer reads pn-reopened, so a close that the filer undoes is not counted'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  'state probe on the PN-R2 rule text, no window: the gate opens when the lever issue closes (no time window) and a flap is bounded by the pn-reopened verify and by the engine demoting a rule after 2 failed cases in 24 hours', 1);

UPDATE control_registry SET evidence = COALESCE(evidence, '') || ' | CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-4 2026-10-26: probed by its control_alternate_probes row (a state probe on the lever the alternate names and on the evidence of the control), judged by the chaos drill, which alone stamps alternate_tested_at.'
WHERE control IN ('research-repo-archive-gate', 'research-repo-sync-switches', 'breach-doctor-caps', 'breach-doctor-taint-guard', 'breach-doctor-action-allowlist', 'breach-doctor-gap-measure', 'breach-doctor-gap-caps', 'breach-doctor-own-issue-guard', 'breach-doctor-strike-cap', 'email-filter-journal-pitch-senders', 'dash-owner-decision-session-gate', 'breach-doctor-auto-demotion', 'breach-doctor-age-gate', 'breach-doctor-tool-exclusion-rule', 'breach-doctor-secret-change-measure', 'breach-doctor-rearm-capacity', 'metric-playbook-recovery-hold', 'pn-r2-filer-quiet-gate') AND instr(COALESCE(evidence, ''), 'CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-4') = 0;

INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'rem-a3-drills',
  'a control alternate counts as tested only while a probe on its own evidence keeps passing, so the fix for 18 controls with no probe is 18 probes that can fail, not 18 dates. A probe is checked against live before it is written, and a probe that fails on live is corrected to measure what the control says and not loosened until it passes',
  'CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-4: one falsifiable read-only probe for each of 18 controls (research-repo-archive-gate, research-repo-sync-switches, email-filter-journal-pitch-senders, dash-owner-decision-session-gate, pn-r2-filer-quiet-gate, metric-playbook-recovery-hold, breach-doctor-caps, -taint-guard, -action-allowlist, -gap-measure, -gap-caps, -own-issue-guard, -strike-cap, -auto-demotion, -age-gate, -tool-exclusion-rule, -secret-change-measure, -rearm-capacity), no alternate_tested_at written, one evidence note per control, one backup table',
  'live qnfo-audit 2026-10-26 18:10-18:40Z: v_control_alternate_untested.controls_untested_without_probe 18 (probes_total 54, probes_enabled 50, probes_failing 3), the 18 controls drill_state no-probe with alternate_tested_at NULL, fm-control-alternate-undrilled reading fail, control_alternate_probes control-alternate-probes last_observed "a control with an alternate has no probe and no tested date" at 13:01Z. All 18 new probes read ok on live read-only (two first drafts failed on live and were corrected: a table name read as a write target, and a rule applied to two older filters of another family). The offline suite breaks every clause of every probe on a fixture of the live schemas and the real chaosJudge reads each reason',
  'migration merged, the next 6-hourly drill runs the 18 probes',
  'eighteen rows of control_alternate_probes (INSERT OR IGNORE), one appended evidence note on eighteen control_registry rows, one backup table, one decision row, read by the drill and the views v_control_alternate_status and v_control_alternate_untested only. No worker, trigger, cron, playbook or ops_config change',
  'the Rollback header removes the probe rows that never ran, removes the evidence note and clears alternate_tested_at for the 18 controls (decision_log stays: append-only)',
  'every control with an alternate has a probe, so the fleet can tell which alternates are proven by a recent pass instead of by a registered sentence, and a new control without one is caught by the hourly detector',
  'v_control_alternate_untested.controls_untested_without_probe reads 0 on apply and fm-control-alternate-undrilled reads pass, the next drill stamps the controls whose probe passes and closes issue 1000214, and a probe that fails files one CHAOS-DRILL-FAILED-1 control issue for that control only',
  'none',
  'd1:qnfo-audit control_registry, v_control_alternate_status, v_control_alternate_untested, control_alternate_probes, ops_config, breach_playbooks, breach_diagnoses, breach_diagnosis_events, agent_issues, metric_registry, analytics_metric_triggers, analytics_action_log, remediation_contracts, email_filters, portfolio_actions, research_run_ledger, cloud_ops_events, sqlite_master (SELECT only, each probe run before it was written), qnfo-fleet-control/worker.js chaosDrill and bdConfig, offline node:sqlite suite with mutation checks'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM decision_log WHERE instr(action, 'CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-4:') = 1);
